g your  yourself expensive urine if you take  probiotics you're just giving your  yourself expensive poop so you need  you know for a probiotic you only need  these in special circumstances  especially you know the really high  potent ones you know if you have an  ongoing gi  disorder there's a new one out for ibs  called um  holy ghost or holly goss is a new one  that's  um being on the market for um ibs  um you know for specific specific  situations there are  probiotics but for a daily general use  you do not need to take them  well that's good information thank you  so much we have time for one more  question  actually we have a couple more coming in  let me let me go ahead and give you  these last two  how can one introduce microbiome into  lung cancer  cell lines that are in vitro studies  so so in vitro studies  you're probably talking about the  anaerobic nature of a lot of these  microbes  so there are certain ways  that you can set up your cell lines in  an anaerobic  chamber some of these anaerobes  depending on what kind they are will  last for about 24 hours in cell culture  and uh norm oxia conditions but you can  also set up  organoid cultures so my colleagues at um  baylor college of medicine rob britton  um and his former postdoc jennifer  octune um he's now i think at utah or  ohio  um actually set up these conditions  where you can actually  culture anaerobic bacteria with  um normal or cancerous um  monoculture cell alliance and they've  got that system working out  uh pretty well and in my studies you  know what i'm actually using is just the  outer membrane vesicles so we don't have  to worry  about you know oxygenation at that point  we can just you know take out the outer  membrane vesicles  and then expose them to the cells but  there's  several people um cindy sears lab rob  britain's lab  jennifer rockton have worked out these  properties to  co-culture anaerobes with  standard cell lines thank you so much  our last question is there a hug